    "body": "**Hands-on check on macOS, release build of this branch (Setups page → \"Lay on a plane\").**\n\n- **`cube_inside_out.stl`:** pick the top face with G17. Apply is greyed out. Its tooltip reads \"…belongs to a body whose facets are inside-out (wound inward), so its outside would be read backwards - fix the model's facet winding (re-export it) before aligning to it\". The \"outside:\" line is absent.\n- **A normal part (the simple2 plate):** the same pick with G17 gives an active Apply (\"Turn the part so the pick lies on G17 (XY)\") and the line \"outside: +Z in the model of face …\".\n\nThe 3-2-1 \"Align WCS\" path was not exercised by hand. It is pinned in `winding_align`.\n\n**Gate:** upstream/main merged (clean), then `scripts/gate.sh quick`. `winding_align` passes 9/9. The remaining reds also fail on upstream main:\n- `swarf_pose_continuity`, fixed by #351;\n- the GPU headless tests.\n",
